REM Protects a semicolon-introduced comment right after every block-boundary marker -- a
REM method's own end marker, a class's end marker, an interface's end marker, and both
REM branches of a DEF FN -- at end of file and mid-stream (with more content following on
REM the same line or the next), in upper, lower and mixed case.

CLASS PUBLIC Gadget
METHOD PUBLIC VOID paint()
x=1
METHODEND; REM comment right after a method's own end marker, mid-stream, upper case
METHOD PUBLIC VOID resize()
y=1
MethodEnd; Rem comment right after a method's own end marker, mixed case, mid-stream
CLASSEND; rem comment right after the class end marker, lower case, mid-stream

INTERFACE PUBLIC Sizable
METHOD PUBLIC VOID grow()
INTERFACEEND; REM comment right after the interface end marker, upper case

DEF FnSquare(n)=n*n; rem comment right after a single-line DEF FN, lower case

DEF FnCube(n)
RETURN n*n*n
FNEND; REM comment right after a multi-line DEF FN's end marker, upper case
